            {
              "id": "55423401-ed07-3f34-8963-6ce4bea71b02",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source expressions are both derived from identifiers, and dataflow analysis indicates that the destination may alias the source. Additionally, there are no explicit checks to ensure that the source and destination do not overlap, and both may be null at the call site, which further increases the risk of undefined behavior. The operation does not use a count based on the destination's capacity, and there are no guards or explicit null-termination after the copy. These factors together indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue that could lead to memory corruption or crashes if the overlap occurs.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory, ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. If overlap is possible, use a function that safely handles overlapping regions, such as `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. Additionally, add explicit checks to ensure that neither the source nor the destination pointers are null before performing the copy operation. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif (timesParameterGradientData.data() != nullptr && cpuArrayViewBuffer != nullptr) {\n    // Use memmove if overlap is possible\n    memmove(timesParameterGradientData.data(), cpuArrayViewBuffer, timesParam.Shape().TotalSize() * sizeof(ElementType));\n}\n```\n\nThis change ensures that the copy operation is safe even if the memory regions overlap, and avoids undefined behavior due to null pointers.\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
                ]
              }
